    "description_raw": "An invisible but tangible field of force surrounds the subject of a mage armor spell, providing a +4 armor bonus to AC.\n\nUnlike mundane armor, mage armor entails no armor check penalty, arcane spell failure chance, or speed reduction. Since mage armor is made of force, incorporeal creatures can't bypass it the way they do normal armor.Mythic Mage ArmorSource Mythic Adventures pg. 100\nThe armor bonus increases to +6. There is a 50% chance that any critical hit or sneak attack made against the target is negated and treated as a normal hit, as if the target were wearing moderate fortification armor.",
